        },
        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/shell-quoting-breakout-command-injection",
          "ruleIndex": 2,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Shell quoting breakout / command injection — Ruled out: interactive.py (shell.run(f'/bin/bash -c \"{cmd}\"'))\n\nThe only input source is the operator typing at the `agentcore$` prompt; per engagement rules, intended execution of commands supplied by an authorized shell user is not a vulnerability. The double-quote-framing is a reliability bug (commands containing `\"` are misparsed), not a trust-boundary violation — no untrusted party can reach this input path in the shipped code."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "interactive.py (shell.run(f'/bin/bash -c \"{cmd}\"'))"
                }
